OL,3,GNEWSAWomen invited to join periods
OL,4,Aresearch project
OL,5,
OL,6,FResearchers in Bradford hope up to
OL,7,F3,000 women in the district will take
OL,8,Fpart in a major study on periods and
OL,9,Fthe menstrual cycle.
OL,11,FThe CycleTrack project, run by health
OL,12,Fresearch organisation Born in Bradford
OL,13,F(BiB), aims to determine why some women
OL,14,Fexperience more difficult periods than
OL,15,Fothers and how they can receive faster
OL,16,Fdiagnoses and more effective treatment.
OL,18,FIt will include women aged 18 and over
OL,19,Fwho experience normal periods, as well
OL,20,Fas those living with pain, heavy
OL,21,Fbleeding and conditions such as
OL,22,Fendometriosis and fibroids.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,382,380,200,160,0,100
